{"name":"Asher Benjamin","hex":"#45575e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"asher","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the alt.suicide.holiday newsgroup, which deals with the topics of suicide and depression."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/asher"},{"term":"benjamin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A balsamic resin from the bark of Styrax trees used in perfumes, incense, and medicine; benzoin resin.","A type of tree which produces benzoin or has similar properties; specifically, Styrax benzoin, Lindera benzoin; a Benjamin bush."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of upper coat for men."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/benjamin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Asher Benjamin","blocks":[{"text":"Asher Benjamin was an American architect and author whose work transitioned between Federal architecture and the later Greek Revival architecture. His seven handbooks on design deeply influenced the look of cities and towns throughout New England until the Civil War. Builders also copied his plans in the Midwest and in the South."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/AsherBenjamine_ca1830_attribChesterHarding_5CollegeMuseums_HistoricDeerfield.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asher_Benjamin","wikidata":"Q691987"},{"title":"Asher","blocks":[{"text":"Asher, in the Book of Genesis, was the younger of the two sons of Jacob and Zilpah, who was the handmaid of Jacob's wife Leah, and Jacob's eighth son overall. He was the founder of the Israelite Tribe of Asher."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Asher_%28Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n%29.jpg/330px-Asher_%28Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asher","wikidata":"Q1775026"},{"title":"Benjamin","blocks":[{"text":"Benjamin was the younger of the two sons of Jacob and Rachel, and Jacob's twelfth and youngest son overall in Jewish, Christian and Islamic tradition. He was also considered the progenitor of the Israelite Tribe of Benjamin. Unlike Rachel's first son, Joseph, Benjamin was born in Canaan according to biblical narrative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Benjamin_%28after_Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n%29.jpg/330px-Benjamin_%28after_Francisco_de_Zurbar%C3%A1n%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin","wikidata":"Q460763"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Mouldings_at_Large_Asher_Benjamin.jpeg/500px-Mouldings_at_Large_Asher_Benjamin.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Mouldings_at_Large_Asher_Benjamin.jpeg/500px-Mouldings_at_Large_Asher_Benjamin.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Mouldings at large,\" from The American Builder's Companion, 1816","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMouldings_at_Large_Asher_Benjamin.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Asher_Benjamin%2C_House_Design.jpg/330px-Asher_Benjamin%2C_House_Design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Asher_Benjamin%2C_House_Design.jpg/330px-Asher_Benjamin%2C_House_Design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Federal style house, from The Country Builder's Assistant, 1797","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAsher_Benjamin%2C_House_Design.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Greenfield_Public_Library%2C_Greenfield%2C_MA.jpg/500px-Greenfield_Public_Library%2C_G